# Web app build-time configuration.
#
# Only variables prefixed VITE_ reach the browser, and they are INLINED into the
# bundle at build time — so these belong wherever you run `vite build`, not
# wherever the files are served. Never put a secret in one: anything here is
# readable by anyone who opens devtools.
#
# In development you need none of this. Leave it unset and the app calls the
# relative `/api`, which Vite proxies to localhost:3031.

# Absolute URL of the API, used only when the API is on a different origin than
# the web app. No trailing slash, and it must include the /api path prefix.
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.calendar.example.com/api
